IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa19-regulative`

-- coa19-tests-regulative.l4: traces of the regulative rules of coa19-regulative.l4. A DEONTIC value cannot be compared in an #ASSERT on the stable binary,
-- so no assertion is written here and check.sh counts none: each trace is run and its outcome is recorded in NOTES.md ("Regulative traces") and compared by eye on the two stable builds.
-- The expected outcome is written beside each trace from the text, BEFORE the run:
--   an act on or before the last day (WITHIN counts inclusively): FULFILLED
--   an act after the last day, or the clock moving past it with nothing done: DEONTIC BREACHED, with the BECAUSE string of the rule

§ `Traces: the duties with a person, an act and a period`

§§ `s 859K(2)(a) and s 871(1): notice to the registrar within 7 days`
-- expected: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 859K(2)(a) the person must give notice to the registrar within 7 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 859K the person who obtains the order or makes the appointment` DOES `s 859K gives notice to the registrar of the order or appointment` AT 7
-- expected: BREACH ("no notice to the registrar within 7 days ... an offence under section 859K(6)")
#TRACE `s 859K(2)(a) the person must give notice to the registrar within 7 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 859K the person who obtains the order or makes the appointment` DOES `s 859K gives notice to the registrar of the order or appointment` AT 8
-- expected: BREACH (nothing done and the clock passes day 7)
#TRACE `s 859K(2)(a) the person must give notice to the registrar within 7 days` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 8
-- expected: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 871(1) the person must give notice of the fact to the registrar within 7 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 859K the person who obtains the order or makes the appointment` DOES `s 859K gives notice to the registrar of the order or appointment` AT 3
-- expected: BREACH ("an offence under section 871(4)")
#TRACE `s 871(1) the person must give notice of the fact to the registrar within 7 days` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 9

§§ `s 859K(3)(a): notice on ceasing to act (no period in the text)`
-- expected: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 859K(3)(a) the person must, on ceasing to act, give notice to the registrar` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 859K the person who obtains the order or makes the appointment` DOES `s 859K gives notice to the registrar that the receiver or manager has ceased to act` AT 40
-- expected: the standing obligation, printed back (no deadline, so a late clock is not a breach)
#TRACE `s 859K(3)(a) the person must, on ceasing to act, give notice to the registrar` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 400

§§ `ss 860(1), 862(2), 878(1), 880(2): particulars and instrument within 21 days`
-- expected: FULFILLED (day 21 is the last day)
#TRACE `s 860(1) the company must deliver the prescribed particulars and the instrument within the period allowed` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 860 the company that creates or acquires the charge` DOES `s 860 delivers the prescribed particulars and the instrument to the registrar` AT 21
-- expected: BREACH ("an offence under section 860(4)")
#TRACE `s 860(1) the company must deliver the prescribed particulars and the instrument within the period allowed` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 860 the company that creates or acquires the charge` DOES `s 860 delivers the prescribed particulars and the instrument to the registrar` AT 22
-- expected: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 862(2) the company must deliver the prescribed particulars and a certified copy within the period allowed` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 860 the company that creates or acquires the charge` DOES `s 860 delivers the prescribed particulars and the instrument to the registrar` AT 10
-- expected: BREACH ("an offence under section 862(4)")
#TRACE `s 862(2) the company must deliver the prescribed particulars and a certified copy within the period allowed` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 22
-- expected: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 878(1) the company must deliver the prescribed particulars and a certified copy within the period allowed` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 860 the company that creates or acquires the charge` DOES `s 860 delivers the prescribed particulars and the instrument to the registrar` AT 21
-- expected: BREACH ("an offence under section 878(4)")
#TRACE `s 878(1) the company must deliver the prescribed particulars and a certified copy within the period allowed` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 860 the company that creates or acquires the charge` DOES `s 860 delivers the prescribed particulars and the instrument to the registrar` AT 30
-- expected: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 880(2) the company must deliver the prescribed particulars and a certified copy within the period allowed` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 860 the company that creates or acquires the charge` DOES `s 860 delivers the prescribed particulars and the instrument to the registrar` AT 1
-- expected: BREACH ("an offence under section 880(3)")
#TRACE `s 880(2) the company must deliver the prescribed particulars and a certified copy within the period allowed` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 40

§§ `s 868(3)(b): the registrar sends the other copy and the certificate within 7 days`
-- expected: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 868(3)(b) the registrar must send the other copy and the certificate to the company within 7 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 868 the registrar` DOES `s 868 sends the other copy and the certificate of registration to the company` AT 7
-- expected: BREACH
#TRACE `s 868(3)(b) the registrar must send the other copy and the certificate to the company within 7 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 868 the registrar` DOES `s 868 sends the other copy and the certificate of registration to the company` AT 8

§§ `ss 859Q(3), 877(3), 892(3): notice of the place where the documents are kept`
-- expected: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 859Q(3) the company must give notice to the registrar of the place within 14 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 860 the company that creates or acquires the charge` DOES `s 859Q gives notice to the registrar of the place where the documents are kept` AT 14
-- expected: BREACH ("an offence under section 859Q(5), 877(5) or 892(5)")
#TRACE `s 859Q(3) the company must give notice to the registrar of the place within 14 days` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 15
